/-!
# Peterfalvi I §2, Step 5 (`|V| ≥ 8` forces `|V| = 8`)

`V = Inv(G) ∪ {1}` is elementary abelian of order `2 ^ m`.  This file proves that if `V` contains
a subgroup `U` of order `8` whose `4`-subgroups have `2`-group centralizers, then `V = U`, so that
`|V| = 8`.  This is Step 5 of the Proposition of Peterfalvi I §2 (p. 191): Wagner's proposition
supplies a Frobenius group `C₇ ⋊ C₃` in `N_G(U)/C_G(U)`, Schur–Zassenhaus splits it off
`C_G(U)`, and Appendix VII then shows that `V` is generated by centralizers lying in `U`.
-/

